1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,550
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,550 --> 00:00:04,840
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,840 --> 00:00:05,830
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,150 --> 00:00:07,770
I've been fixing
appliances

5
00:00:07,770 --> 00:00:09,170
for thirty years.

6
00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:11,410
Kneeling behind washers
and fridges

7
00:00:11,410 --> 00:00:12,940
in people's homes,

8
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:14,060
all day long.

9
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:15,220
I had my right knee

10
00:00:15,220 --> 00:00:16,860
replaced two years ago.

11
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:18,880
It has hurt every day
since.

12
00:00:19,090 --> 00:00:20,520
Not surgery pain.

13
00:00:20,830 --> 00:00:22,180
I know what that felt
like,

14
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:23,200
and it went away.

15
00:00:23,510 --> 00:00:24,440
This is different.

16
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:24,880
Tight.

17
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:25,430
Full.

18
00:00:25,470 --> 00:00:26,400
Like a band around

19
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,180
the joint that never
loosens.

20
00:00:28,380 --> 00:00:29,440
And for two years I've

21
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:30,730
been told the same thing.

22
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:32,130
Give it time.

23
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:34,330
At six weeks it was
swelling,

24
00:00:34,330 --> 00:00:35,700
and swelling is normal.

25
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:36,720
At three months,

26
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:37,790
give it six.

27
00:00:37,910 --> 00:00:39,050
At six months,

28
00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:40,670
some knees take a full
year.

29
00:00:41,070 --> 00:00:41,670
At a year,

30
00:00:41,670 --> 00:00:43,610
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

31
00:00:43,890 --> 00:00:45,220
And I didn't just wait.

32
00:00:45,410 --> 00:00:46,950
We went down the list.

33
00:00:47,110 --> 00:00:48,610
More physical therapy.

34
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:49,810
Every session,

35
00:00:49,810 --> 00:00:51,320
every exercise at home.

36
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:52,650
I got stronger.

37
00:00:52,690 --> 00:00:54,060
The tightness never moved.

38
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:55,850
The pain pills helped,

39
00:00:55,850 --> 00:00:57,120
and that was the problem.

40
00:00:57,330 --> 00:00:59,170
I'm already on enough
every morning,

41
00:00:59,170 --> 00:01:00,070
and nobody could tell me

42
00:01:00,070 --> 00:01:01,140
when I'd get to stop.

43
00:01:01,430 --> 00:01:02,870
Then a nerve block.

44
00:01:02,950 --> 00:01:04,740
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

45
00:01:04,820 --> 00:01:06,310
And after that, a second

46
00:01:06,310 --> 00:01:07,310
operation to go back

47
00:01:07,310 --> 00:01:08,330
in and do it over.

48
00:01:08,390 --> 00:01:09,310
I said no.

49
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:10,580
Every morning

50
00:01:10,580 --> 00:01:11,970
I stepped out of bed

51
00:01:11,970 --> 00:01:13,000
and my knee felt like

52
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,710
a band was wrapped around
it,

53
00:01:14,710 --> 00:01:16,820
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

54
00:01:17,290 --> 00:01:18,860
Every morning I took
something

55
00:01:18,860 --> 00:01:20,270
for it and went to work.

56
00:01:20,490 --> 00:01:21,860
Couldn't kneel down to get

57
00:01:21,860 --> 00:01:23,260
behind a dryer,

58
00:01:23,260 --> 00:01:24,870
couldn't do the stairs,

59
00:01:24,870 --> 00:01:25,980
couldn't stand at the
counter

60
00:01:25,980 --> 00:01:27,700
long enough to finish
dinner,

61
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:29,550
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

62
00:01:29,550 --> 00:01:31,460
without shifting every two
minutes.

63
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:32,900
It woke me at night,

64
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:34,690
and it turned ordinary
things,

65
00:01:34,690 --> 00:01:35,960
like getting in the car

66
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:37,380
or up off the couch,

67
00:01:37,380 --> 00:01:38,430
into a decision.

68
00:01:38,610 --> 00:01:40,290
Some days I'd finish a
service call

69
00:01:40,290 --> 00:01:41,430
and sit in the van before
I

70
00:01:41,430 --> 00:01:42,800
could drive to the next
one.

71
00:01:42,950 --> 00:01:44,490
After a long and serious

72
00:01:44,490 --> 00:01:45,710
talk with my wife,

73
00:01:45,710 --> 00:01:47,120
I went back in one more
time.

74
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:48,610
That was the fourth set

75
00:01:48,610 --> 00:01:50,090
of X-rays on this knee.

76
00:01:50,230 --> 00:01:51,810
And like the three before
it,

77
00:01:51,810 --> 00:01:54,020
the answer was everything
looks great.

78
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:56,380
No loosening, no
infection,

79
00:01:56,380 --> 00:01:57,350
nothing wrong.

80
00:01:57,550 --> 00:01:59,090
Only this time

81
00:01:59,090 --> 00:02:00,540
there was no new number.

82
00:02:00,630 --> 00:02:03,160
Nobody said give it
another six months.

83
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:05,060
There was nothing left to
give it.

84
00:02:05,470 --> 00:02:07,210
Thirty years of figuring
out what's

85
00:02:07,210 --> 00:02:08,990
wrong in other people's
homes,

86
00:02:08,990 --> 00:02:10,600
and nobody could tell me

87
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:12,520
what was wrong with my own
knee.

88
00:02:12,660 --> 00:02:13,610
I sat in my van

89
00:02:13,610 --> 00:02:15,430
in the parking lot for a
while.

90
00:02:15,470 --> 00:02:16,490
Okay, I thought.

91
00:02:16,610 --> 00:02:18,010
Then explain this.

92
00:02:18,330 --> 00:02:20,420
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

93
00:02:20,420 --> 00:02:21,870
I hit my breaking point.

94
00:02:22,190 --> 00:02:24,240
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

95
00:02:24,430 --> 00:02:26,370
Everyone in the house was
asleep

96
00:02:26,370 --> 00:02:28,110
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

97
00:02:28,110 --> 00:02:29,220
with my leg up,

98
00:02:29,220 --> 00:02:30,840
trying to find any angle
where

99
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:32,450
it didn't feel like
something was wrapped

100
00:02:32,450 --> 00:02:34,490
around my knee and
tightening.

101
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:37,100
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

102
00:02:37,270 --> 00:02:38,910
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

103
00:02:39,030 --> 00:02:39,970
And I had four service

104
00:02:39,970 --> 00:02:41,290
calls booked in the
morning.

105
00:02:41,510 --> 00:02:42,500
And I just thought,

106
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:44,200
is this really my life
now?

107
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:45,630
I can't live like this.

108
00:02:45,790 --> 00:02:47,520
So I made myself a
promise.

109
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:48,460
I wouldn't go a day

110
00:02:48,460 --> 00:02:50,010
without looking for an
answer.

111
00:02:50,210 --> 00:02:51,480
And when I found one,

112
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:52,570
I'd share it with everyone

113
00:02:52,570 --> 00:02:53,940
going through the same
thing.

114
00:02:54,350 --> 00:02:55,450
So I got my laptop

115
00:02:55,450 --> 00:02:56,630
out and went looking.

116
00:02:56,780 --> 00:02:57,900
Not for a product.

117
00:02:57,940 --> 00:02:59,150
For an explanation.

118
00:02:59,460 --> 00:03:01,010
Mayo Clinic forums,

119
00:03:01,010 --> 00:03:03,210
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

120
00:03:03,210 --> 00:03:04,530
doctor videos,

121
00:03:04,530 --> 00:03:05,630
medical animations.

122
00:03:05,670 --> 00:03:06,580
And that's when I found

123
00:03:06,580 --> 00:03:08,680
a video from a physical
therapist

124
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:09,300
named Dr.

125
00:03:09,340 --> 00:03:11,930
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

126
00:03:11,930 --> 00:03:13,930
had been through exactly
this.

127
00:03:13,970 --> 00:03:16,530
But before I say anything
else,

128
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:18,090
I want to be straight with
you.

129
00:03:18,440 --> 00:03:20,330
You've already had
something work fast.

130
00:03:20,370 --> 00:03:21,270
The ice.

131
00:03:21,310 --> 00:03:23,040
The first week of a new
pill.

132
00:03:23,210 --> 00:03:25,000
The good day after a
session.

133
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:26,220
Then it wore off.

134
00:03:26,390 --> 00:03:28,320
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

135
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:30,280
Fast relief isn't relief.

136
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:31,640
It's a preview.

137
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:32,790
So I'm not going to tell

138
00:03:32,790 --> 00:03:34,090
you this works fast.

139
00:03:34,130 --> 00:03:35,090
It doesn't.

140
00:03:35,230 --> 00:03:37,040
But if you're willing to
be patient,

141
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:38,300
and to look at what's
going

142
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:39,410
on around your new knee

143
00:03:39,410 --> 00:03:41,070
instead of inside it,
there

144
00:03:41,070 --> 00:03:43,440
is a real reason it still
hurts.

145
00:03:43,570 --> 00:03:45,730
And something you can do
about it.

146
00:03:45,990 --> 00:03:47,580
Let me explain what he
said,

147
00:03:47,580 --> 00:03:48,880
because this is what
changed

148
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:50,030
everything for me.

149
00:03:50,180 --> 00:03:51,900
He started with the
basics.

150
00:03:51,990 --> 00:03:53,370
A knee replacement takes
out

151
00:03:53,370 --> 00:03:55,050
the worn joint surfaces

152
00:03:55,050 --> 00:03:57,050
and puts in metal and
plastic.

153
00:03:57,310 --> 00:03:59,030
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

154
00:03:59,030 --> 00:04:00,580
you had before the
operation.

155
00:04:00,970 --> 00:04:02,280
That part I already knew.

156
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:03,880
But then he explained
something

157
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:05,380
nobody had ever told me.

158
00:04:05,420 --> 00:04:06,150
He said,

159
00:04:06,150 --> 00:04:07,450
think about a swollen foot

160
00:04:07,450 --> 00:04:08,560
inside a shoe.

161
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:10,130
The shoe didn't shrink.

162
00:04:10,300 --> 00:04:12,210
Your foot is taking up
more room,

163
00:04:12,210 --> 00:04:13,790
so everything feels
cramped

164
00:04:13,790 --> 00:04:15,130
and tight and squeezed.

165
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:16,430
Your new knee sits

166
00:04:16,430 --> 00:04:18,060
in a limited space with
living

167
00:04:18,060 --> 00:04:19,720
tissue packed all around
it.

168
00:04:20,210 --> 00:04:22,160
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

169
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:23,880
had to work through that
tissue.

170
00:04:24,130 --> 00:04:27,090
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

171
00:04:27,550 --> 00:04:29,100
At first that's normal.

172
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:31,140
But in some people that
swelling can

173
00:04:31,140 --> 00:04:34,100
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

174
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:36,220
And swollen tissue takes
up more

175
00:04:36,220 --> 00:04:38,240
room than calm tissue
does.

176
00:04:38,450 --> 00:04:39,540
So when you bend,

177
00:04:39,540 --> 00:04:41,740
that tissue gets
compressed.

178
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:43,040
When you straighten,

179
00:04:43,040 --> 00:04:44,350
it gets pulled tight.

180
00:04:44,460 --> 00:04:45,480
That's the band.

181
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:47,810
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

182
00:04:47,860 --> 00:04:48,740
And you start being

183
00:04:48,740 --> 00:04:49,870
the one who says,

184
00:04:49,870 --> 00:04:50,590
you go ahead.

185
00:04:50,630 --> 00:04:51,700
I'll stay here.

186
00:04:51,940 --> 00:04:53,820
And that's exactly why so
much

187
00:04:53,820 --> 00:04:56,000
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

188
00:04:56,230 --> 00:04:58,470
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

189
00:04:58,470 --> 00:04:59,430
around the knee.

190
00:04:59,470 --> 00:05:00,290
Worth doing,

191
00:05:00,290 --> 00:05:01,480
and I'd done it.

192
00:05:01,610 --> 00:05:03,240
It does nothing about
tissue

193
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:04,350
taking up room.

194
00:05:04,390 --> 00:05:05,720
A nerve block quiets

195
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:07,410
the nerve carrying the
signal.

196
00:05:07,610 --> 00:05:09,740
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

197
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:12,010
But when that irritated
tissue

198
00:05:12,010 --> 00:05:13,780
finally calms down,

199
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:15,460
it holds less fluid,

200
00:05:15,460 --> 00:05:17,220
and it takes up less room.

201
00:05:17,510 --> 00:05:19,120
Less room taken up means

202
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:21,280
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

203
00:05:21,440 --> 00:05:23,350
That's what takes the
pressure off.

204
00:05:23,620 --> 00:05:25,110
After two years of this,

205
00:05:25,110 --> 00:05:26,680
it finally made sense.

206
00:05:27,020 --> 00:05:28,930
The problem was never the
new knee.

207
00:05:29,070 --> 00:05:30,960
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

208
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:32,810
He calls it the squeeze.

209
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:35,320
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

210
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:37,070
I'd bought knee sleeves,

211
00:05:37,070 --> 00:05:39,340
compression braces,
creams,

212
00:05:39,340 --> 00:05:41,140
half of Amazon really,

213
00:05:41,140 --> 00:05:42,390
and all any of it gave

214
00:05:42,390 --> 00:05:43,470
me was an hour.

215
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:44,830
I even looked at going

216
00:05:44,830 --> 00:05:46,730
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

217
00:05:46,780 --> 00:05:48,840
But at $200 a session

218
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:50,620
with nothing covered by
insurance,

219
00:05:50,620 --> 00:05:51,910
that was a quick no.

220
00:05:51,950 --> 00:05:53,050
Then one night I went

221
00:05:53,050 --> 00:05:54,320
back to that knee
replacement

222
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:55,780
group and actually read
it.

223
00:05:56,050 --> 00:05:57,360
Thousands of people,

224
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:58,980
years out from surgery,

225
00:05:58,980 --> 00:06:01,270
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

226
00:06:01,270 --> 00:06:02,610
nobody could explain.

227
00:06:02,980 --> 00:06:04,700
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

228
00:06:04,700 --> 00:06:06,460
the same thing kept coming
up.

229
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:08,470
This one device,

230
00:06:08,470 --> 00:06:09,970
and people saying it was
the first

231
00:06:09,970 --> 00:06:11,350
thing that made a
difference.

232
00:06:11,650 --> 00:06:13,830
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

233
00:06:13,830 --> 00:06:15,150
alright, here it comes,

234
00:06:15,150 --> 00:06:16,480
he's selling me something,

235
00:06:16,480 --> 00:06:18,120
let me shut that down
right now.

236
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:19,790
I'm only here because I
made myself

237
00:06:19,790 --> 00:06:21,790
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

238
00:06:21,790 --> 00:06:22,710
that if I ever found

239
00:06:22,710 --> 00:06:23,830
something that helped,

240
00:06:23,830 --> 00:06:24,850
I'd say so.

241
00:06:25,430 --> 00:06:27,190
It's called the KenRelief
Red

242
00:06:27,190 --> 00:06:28,540
Light Therapy Wrap.

243
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:30,620
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

244
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:31,980
It looked like the cheap

245
00:06:31,980 --> 00:06:33,760
knee sleeves off Amazon

246
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:35,240
that did nothing for me.

247
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:37,450
But I went to their
website anyway,

248
00:06:37,450 --> 00:06:38,350
just to see what all

249
00:06:38,350 --> 00:06:39,380
the fuss was about.

250
00:06:39,730 --> 00:06:41,750
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

251
00:06:41,750 --> 00:06:44,340
charge $200 a session for,

252
00:06:44,340 --> 00:06:47,180
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

253
00:06:47,180 --> 00:06:48,240
in a wrap you plug

254
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:49,490
into the wall at home.

255
00:06:49,710 --> 00:06:51,310
Two hundred and forty
lights.

256
00:06:51,520 --> 00:06:54,010
Red at 660 nanometers

257
00:06:54,010 --> 00:06:56,650
and near-infrared at 850,

258
00:06:56,650 --> 00:06:59,090
run together for the
strongest effect.

259
00:06:59,130 --> 00:07:00,540
Four strength levels.

260
00:07:00,730 --> 00:07:02,570
A five to thirty minute
timer.

261
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:04,140
Then I saw the guarantee.

262
00:07:04,210 --> 00:07:05,400
Ninety days.

263
00:07:05,450 --> 00:07:07,310
Results or your money
back,

264
00:07:07,310 --> 00:07:09,860
no questions, no store
credit,

265
00:07:09,860 --> 00:07:11,750
and you don't even send it
back.

266
00:07:11,820 --> 00:07:14,230
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

267
00:07:14,230 --> 00:07:15,880
days to change my mind.

268
00:07:15,920 --> 00:07:17,390
There wasn't much to lose,

269
00:07:17,390 --> 00:07:18,410
so I ordered it.

270
00:07:18,450 --> 00:07:19,730
Two of them, actually.

271
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:21,940
Only the right knee was
replaced,

272
00:07:21,940 --> 00:07:24,060
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

273
00:07:24,060 --> 00:07:25,720
and I'd done it for two
years.

274
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:27,840
The left one was carrying
the difference.

275
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:28,490
When it came,

276
00:07:28,490 --> 00:07:30,490
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

277
00:07:30,490 --> 00:07:31,570
because I'd been let down

278
00:07:31,570 --> 00:07:33,440
too many times to get
excited.

279
00:07:33,650 --> 00:07:35,390
What I felt was warmth.

280
00:07:35,640 --> 00:07:37,570
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

281
00:07:37,740 --> 00:07:39,500
More like it was coming
from inside

282
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:41,280
the knee and spreading
around it.

283
00:07:41,490 --> 00:07:42,430
And that was it.

284
00:07:42,470 --> 00:07:44,100
That was the whole
experience.

285
00:07:44,140 --> 00:07:45,280
When I took it off,

286
00:07:45,280 --> 00:07:46,380
I'll be honest,

287
00:07:46,380 --> 00:07:48,080
nothing dramatic had
happened.

288
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:49,770
And after what that video
said,

289
00:07:49,770 --> 00:07:51,520
that's exactly what I
expected.

290
00:07:51,750 --> 00:07:53,180
What was different was

291
00:07:53,180 --> 00:07:54,070
that for the first time

292
00:07:54,070 --> 00:07:55,160
in two years

293
00:07:55,160 --> 00:07:56,870
I'd done something for my
knee

294
00:07:56,870 --> 00:07:57,840
instead of to it.

295
00:07:58,350 --> 00:07:59,310
Twenty minutes,

296
00:07:59,310 --> 00:08:00,420
in my own chair,

297
00:08:00,420 --> 00:08:01,400
after work.

298
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:03,010
No drive, no copay.

299
00:08:03,330 --> 00:08:04,930
They say twenty minutes.

300
00:08:05,050 --> 00:08:06,350
I did thirty,

301
00:08:06,350 --> 00:08:07,260
twice a day,

302
00:08:07,260 --> 00:08:09,040
lowest setting that first
week.

303
00:08:09,180 --> 00:08:10,660
I put it on the calendar.

304
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:11,900
The first week,

305
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:12,720
I couldn't have told

306
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:14,100
you if anything was
happening.

307
00:08:14,140 --> 00:08:15,020
I tried not to get

308
00:08:15,020 --> 00:08:15,900
my hopes up.

309
00:08:16,050 --> 00:08:16,930
I'd had things help

310
00:08:16,930 --> 00:08:18,650
for a week and then stop.

311
00:08:19,050 --> 00:08:20,550
But somewhere in the
second week

312
00:08:20,550 --> 00:08:21,600
I noticed I'd come down

313
00:08:21,600 --> 00:08:23,330
the stairs without holding
the rail.

314
00:08:23,780 --> 00:08:25,050
I hadn't decided to.

315
00:08:25,130 --> 00:08:26,090
I just did it,

316
00:08:26,090 --> 00:08:27,940
then stopped halfway down

317
00:08:27,940 --> 00:08:29,240
because I realized.

318
00:08:29,520 --> 00:08:30,690
By the end of the fourth

319
00:08:30,690 --> 00:08:31,760
week I'd slept through

320
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:33,600
the night four times
running.

321
00:08:33,950 --> 00:08:35,650
I stood at the counter and
finished

322
00:08:35,650 --> 00:08:38,000
making dinner without
looking for the stool.

323
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:39,820
None of that is dramatic.

324
00:08:39,860 --> 00:08:40,880
All of it was gone

325
00:08:40,880 --> 00:08:42,170
for two years.

326
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:43,980
A few weeks later my wife
asked

327
00:08:43,980 --> 00:08:44,900
if I wanted to walk

328
00:08:44,900 --> 00:08:46,530
the long way around the
block.

329
00:08:46,750 --> 00:08:47,710
And for the first time

330
00:08:47,710 --> 00:08:48,510
in two years,

331
00:08:48,510 --> 00:08:49,710
I said yes.

332
00:08:49,780 --> 00:08:51,620
I wanted to understand
why,

333
00:08:51,620 --> 00:08:53,100
so I read the whole thing.

334
00:08:53,140 --> 00:08:54,800
It comes down to four
steps.

335
00:08:54,840 --> 00:08:55,470
One.

336
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:57,010
The tissue around a new

337
00:08:57,010 --> 00:08:58,950
knee can stay inflamed

338
00:08:58,950 --> 00:09:01,390
long after surgery is
over.

339
00:09:01,430 --> 00:09:02,070
Two.

340
00:09:02,110 --> 00:09:04,730
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

341
00:09:04,730 --> 00:09:05,730
so it takes up more

342
00:09:05,730 --> 00:09:06,770
room than it should.

343
00:09:06,810 --> 00:09:07,570
Three.

344
00:09:07,830 --> 00:09:09,170
There's only so much room
in there.

345
00:09:09,210 --> 00:09:10,690
Bending compresses it.

346
00:09:10,870 --> 00:09:12,510
Straightening pulls it
tight.

347
00:09:12,660 --> 00:09:13,890
That's the squeeze.

348
00:09:13,930 --> 00:09:14,620
Four.

349
00:09:15,050 --> 00:09:17,180
Red and near-infrared
light

350
00:09:17,180 --> 00:09:19,790
have been studied for
calming that inflammation,

351
00:09:19,790 --> 00:09:21,040
so the swelling and the
pressure

352
00:09:21,040 --> 00:09:22,270
can come down with it.

353
00:09:22,580 --> 00:09:23,680
In a randomized trial,

354
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:25,400
patients given light
therapy after

355
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:26,530
a knee replacement

356
00:09:26,530 --> 00:09:28,850
had less pain, less
swelling

357
00:09:28,850 --> 00:09:30,400
and better early movement

358
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:31,630
than those who weren't.

359
00:09:32,210 --> 00:09:35,520
A 2025 review said the
same,

360
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:36,660
and was clear the evidence

361
00:09:36,660 --> 00:09:37,660
is still limited.

362
00:09:37,970 --> 00:09:39,820
I probably sound like a
broken record

363
00:09:39,820 --> 00:09:41,880
to my family and my
customers.

364
00:09:42,220 --> 00:09:43,710
But after two years of
doing

365
00:09:43,710 --> 00:09:45,400
everything I was told

366
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:47,170
and getting nowhere,

367
00:09:47,170 --> 00:09:48,830
you have no idea what it's
like

368
00:09:48,830 --> 00:09:50,390
to sleep through the
night,

369
00:09:50,390 --> 00:09:51,990
say yes to the walk,

370
00:09:51,990 --> 00:09:53,530
and get my life back.

371
00:09:53,750 --> 00:09:55,080
So take it from me.

372
00:09:55,130 --> 00:09:56,690
Don't spend another year
waiting

373
00:09:56,690 --> 00:09:57,670
for it to settle.

374
00:09:57,890 --> 00:09:59,770
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

375
00:10:00,020 --> 00:10:01,440
More than ten thousand
people

376
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:02,480
with pain after a knee

377
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:04,390
replacement have already
tried this.

378
00:10:04,510 --> 00:10:06,120
Some had it worse than I
did.

379
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:07,530
You can get the KenRelief

380
00:10:07,530 --> 00:10:08,870
wrap from their website,

381
00:10:08,870 --> 00:10:10,210
with a discount link

382
00:10:10,210 --> 00:10:11,630
and ninety days to try it.

383
00:10:12,070 --> 00:10:13,780
If it doesn't do anything
for you,

384
00:10:13,780 --> 00:10:15,150
you get your money back

385
00:10:15,150 --> 00:10:16,320
and you keep the wrap.

386
00:10:16,410 --> 00:10:17,700
They only release so many

387
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:18,730
at that price.

388
00:10:18,980 --> 00:10:20,280
If it's still there,

389
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:21,370
get one,

390
00:10:21,370 --> 00:10:22,960
and stop the squeeze.

